 61CU    28SI(36AR,3PG)                2008AN06                  15NDS    201503
 61CU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=KAZIMIERZ ZUBER, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 125, 1 (2015)$       
 61CU2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61CU c  2008An06: Three experiments were performed: GS54, GSFMA42 and          
 61CU2c  GSFMA138. All experiments used the GAMMASPHERE array to measure        
 61CU3c  E|g, I|g, |g|g, (particle)|g coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO). The protons and |a   
 61CU4c  particles were detected using the MICROBALL array and Si strip         
 61CU5c  telescopes used for |DE-E measurements. Comparisons with cranked       
 61CU6c  Nilsson and Strutinsky model calculations for collective structures    
 61CU7c  and with large-scale shell-model calculations for normal-deformed      
 61CU8c  states.                                                                
 61CU t  ---------------------------------------------------------------------- 
 61CU t  Experiment          GS54           GSFMA42              GSFMA138       
 61CU t  ---------------------------------------------------------------------- 
 61CU t  Beam energy   143 MeV                 148 MeV                 142 MeV  
 61CU t  Target thick.  0.42 mg/cm{+2}     0.42 mg/cm{+2}     0.2 mg/cm{+2}     
 61CU t  Support foil   0.9 mg/cm{+2} Ta   1.0 mg/cm{+2} Au   1.1 mg/cm{+2} Ta  
 61CU t  ---------------------------------------------------------------------- 
 61CU t  Germanium         82 detectors    86 detectors         77 detectors    
 61CU t  Microball             95 elements     65 elements          16 elements 
 61CU t  Si |DE-E telescopes   --                  4                 8          
 61CU t  Liquid scintillators  15 detectors    20 detectors         30 detectors
 61CU t  (neutron shell)                                                        
 61CU t  Laboratory            LBNL            Argonne              Argonne     
 61CU t  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
 61CU cG $DCO values are for 30|'-83|' geometry with gates on |DJ=2,            
 61CU2cG quadrupole and |DJ=1, dipole transitions. Expected values of DCOs      
 61CU3cG are: 1. for gate on |DJ=2, quadrupole: 1.0 for |DJ=2, quadrupole;      
 61CU4cG |<1.0 for |DJ=0 and |?0.6 for |DJ=1 transitions. 2. for gate on        
 61CU5cG |DJ=1, dipole transitions: |?1.0 for |DJ=1, dipole; 1.7 for |DJ=2,     
 61CU6cG quadrupole or |DJ=0, dipole.                                           
 61CU cG $DCO(1) corresponds to value for gate on |DJ=2, quadrupole             
 61CU cG $DCO(2) corresponds to value for gate on |DJ=1, dipole, except         
 61CU2cG for one case where the value is for gate on |DJ=0                      
 61CU3cG transition, as indicated.                                              
 61CU cG RI$Relative to 100 for 1310.4|g measured in the {+28}Si({+36}Ar,3p|g)  
 61CU2cG reaction (2008An06).                                                   
 61CU cG M$Deduced from DCO measurements in 2008An06. In the absence of         
 61CU2cG polarization or other confirming data, the evaluators assign           
 61CU3cG Mult=Q for |DJ=2,quadrupole transitions, mult=D or D+Q for |DJ=1 or    
 61CU4cG 0 dipole or dipole+quadrupole transitions. From systematics and band   
 61CU5cG assignments, 2008An06 assign E2 for all |DJ=2 transitions and          
 61CU6cG M1+E2, M1 or E1 for |DJ=1 or 0 transitions                             
 61CU cG E(X)$DCO value is for an unresolved doublet                            
 61CU cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g data                                   
 61CU cL J$Spin-parities of high-spin states (>9/2) are assigned from           
 61CU2cL |g|g(|q) and band structure (2008An06). Assignments of low-spin        
 61CU3cL levels are from Adopted Levels.                                        
 61CU cL J(n)$From Fig. 1 of 2008An06, not given in authors' table 2.           
